  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member opening someone's profile in SwiftHFR, I want the profile sheet to load, so that I can read it. Since 2026-11-26 HFR refuses profile pages to anonymous requests (403), and SwiftHFR fetches profiles without cookies on purpose (LOT-116), so every profile now fails.\n\n### Facts (measured 2026-11-27, mac/mac-mbp, read-only GETs)\n- `GET /hfr/profil-<id>.htm` with no cookie: **403**, Apache's default page (230 bytes), as on #1349.\n- The same URL with a logged-in kit session (`user1`, cookies `md_id`, `md_passs`, `md_user` from `login_validation.php`): **200**, 7.4 KB, a real profile page.\n- Legacy fixed it on `master` in `bb58131d` (2026-11-26, #1349): `UserProfileService` sends the main account's cookies on the request (`httpShouldHandleCookies = false`), refuses to send with no account (`loginRequired`), maps 401/403 to `accessDenied` (`HFRswift/Swift/UserProfileService.swift:14-50` @ `bb58131d`).\n- SwiftHFR: `App/SwiftHFR/Profile/UserProfileSource.swift:24` calls `fetcher.profile(memberID:as: .anonymous)` (LOT-116 differences 1-2, #124: the parser was only verified on logged-out pages).\n\n### Scope\n1. Capture: a logged-in profile page (the LOT-116 states the parser covers), anonymized, so the parser is verified on it (LESSONS 35-36); HFR-PROTOCOL note on the 403.\n2. Send the current account's session for the profile request; with no account, show a \"log in to see profiles\" state instead of a request; a 401/403 becomes its own error, not « Profil impossible à lire ».\n3. Update the LOT-116 spec's differences 1-2 and the GAP row if one exists (`### Ledger`).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- Parser tests green on the logged-in capture; a test that the request carries the session and that no request leaves without an account (fails without the change).\n- Session and cookie code: Opus or Fable review, merged by cloud/orch (AGENTS.md §8).\n\nRefs #1349 (legacy), #124.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
